required_documents:
VIA APPLY@UNITO (applicants with a foreign qualification):
1) Valid ID card (Italian/EU citizens and equivalent) or valid passport (non-EU citizens);
2) For non-EU citizens legally residing in Italy: a residence permit valid for university enrolment;
3) The first-cycle (bachelor's) degree certificate / final qualification, with proof of authenticity;
4) Transcript of records / academic transcript showing exams and credits - needed to demonstrate the 18-CFU curricular requirement across at least two SSD blocks;
5) MOTIVATION LETTER in English (explicitly listed under 'Other requirements' on the AGIC course page; UNITO's general rule allows English or Italian for postgraduate programmes);
6) English language certificate from the accepted list (or a medium-of-instruction letter from the previous university);
7) Second-language certificate / university language exam certificate at A2 or above, where available;
8) Optional but recommended: degree programme syllabus (course descriptions) issued by the foreign institution, with translation;
9) Declaration of Value, CIMEA Statement of Verification / Statement of Comparability - not always mandatory at application but may be requested by the International Students Office, and useful to speed up enrolment;
10) Certified translation into Italian, English, French or Spanish for any document not issued in one of those four languages (entry-qualification documents are accepted in English, French, Italian or Spanish);
11) Payment of the non-refundable EUR 60 application fee within the deadline of the call (the same amount whether one or two programmes are selected).
Incomplete applications are not considered, and documents without signature, seal or stamp are not accepted. The University may request additional documents both after submission and at the enrolment step.

VIA MYUNITO (applicants with an Italian qualification, registering for the admission interview): self-certification of the degree held or of enrolment in a bachelor's programme, listing exams taken (required); motivation letter in English (required); CV in English (required); English and second-language (or university language exam) certificates, if already held. Applicants holding a qualification from an Italian university other than UNITO must first obtain temporary 'prospective student' credentials through MyUniTo.

AT ENROLMENT (non-EU visa applicants): Universitaly pre-enrolment application validated by the University, study visa, and residence permit documentation. [uncertain]
